### Current vs. Expected behavior


### Actual Behavior

The GitHub OAuth flow redirects to:

https://example.com/api/auth/callback/github

The production callback handles the link directly. `/oauth-proxy-callback` is never called.

This means a user starting the flow from a preview/local deployment does not return to that preview/local origin through the proxy flow.

### Expected Behavior

`linkSocial` should work with `oAuthProxy` the same way social sign-in does.

For preview/local origins, the flow should eventually redirect to something like:

https://preview.example.com/api/auth/oauth-proxy-callback?callbackURL=...

so the linked account/session behavior is completed on the origin where the flow started.

