### Reproduction

1. Configure Better Auth's Apple provider as shown in the [Apple authentication docs](https://better-auth.com/docs/authentication/apple), alongside other social providers (Google, Discord) in the same instance.
2. Configure a Services ID in Apple Developer with the deployed return URL and verify the domain.
3. Click "Sign in with Apple" from the deployed site. Better Auth redirects the browser to:
   ```
   https://appleid.apple.com/auth/authorize?response_type=code+id_token&client_id=com.example.app.si&state=<random-state-token>&scope=email+name&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.example.com%2Fapi%2Fauth%2Fcallback%2Fapple&response_mode=form_post
   ```
4. Authenticate at `appleid.apple.com`.
5. Apple submits a `form_post` redirect to `/api/auth/callback/apple`. Better Auth's callback handler 302-redirects POST → GET so cookies are sent (`packages/better-auth/src/api/routes/callback.ts:42-58`), which is the GET observed in the server logs below.
6. Observe a `State mismatch: verification not found` error in the server logs and that the user is not signed in.

Other social providers (Google, Discord) configured on the same Better Auth instance, using the same `secondaryStorage`, do not exhibit this bug.

### Current vs. Expected behavior

**Current:** Web sign-in fails on the OAuth callback every time. The OAuth flow completes at Apple's end, the browser is redirected back, but the callback handler cannot find the verification record and rejects:

```
GET 302 /api/auth/callback/apple
ERROR [Better Auth]: Failed to parse state [Error [BetterAuthError]: State mismatch: verification not found] {
  code: 'state_mismatch',
  details: [Object]
}
ERROR [Better Auth]: Failed to parse state [Error [BetterAuthError]: State mismatch: verification not found] {
  code: 'state_mismatch',
  details: [Object]
}
```

**Expected:** Apple Sign In on web should succeed end-to-end with the configuration shown in the docs (or, if extra configuration is required, it should fail in a way that points at the actual cause).

