### Additional context

What we have looked at trying to understand this:

- The error message `"State mismatch: verification not found"` is thrown by `parseGenericState` in `packages/better-auth/src/state.ts:194`, when `findVerificationValue(state)` returns `null` in the database storage strategy path.
- The [`state_mismatch` errors page](https://better-auth.com/docs/reference/errors/state_mismatch) lists "Secondary storage (Redis / KV) without database fallback" as cause #3 — when `secondaryStorage` is configured and `verification.storeInDatabase` is not `true`, verification records are written only to secondary storage, and `findVerificationValue` returns `null` on a secondary-storage miss without ever checking the database. Our config matches that shape.
- We have already applied the workaround in [#5243](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/issues/5243) (`defaultCookieAttributes: { sameSite: 'none', secure: true }` in production), and the bug still reproduces.
- Other social providers (Google, Discord) configured on the same Better Auth instance, using the same `secondaryStorage`, do not exhibit this bug. They sign in successfully every time.
- Apple's authorize URL uses `response_mode=form_post` (set unconditionally by the Apple provider in `packages/core/src/social-providers/apple.ts:102`), so its callback comes in as a cross-site POST. Better Auth's callback handler 302-redirects this to GET (`packages/better-auth/src/api/routes/callback.ts:42-58`) before reaching `parseState`.

What does not fit cleanly with the existing diagnoses:

- The docs frame cause #3 as an *occasional* failure ("if the key is evicted"). What we observe is **100% failure on every Apple attempt**, with no failures at all on Google or Discord using the same `secondaryStorage`. That points at something more deterministic than KV eviction or memory pressure.
- We have not been able to identify what makes Apple specifically reach a state where the verification record is missing on lookup, while Google and Discord do not.

Related issues that describe the same surface symptom:

- [#5243 — OAuth providers fail with `state_mismatch` error when using POST callbacks](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/issues/5243)
- [#5227 — state mismatch in apple sign in](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/issues/5227)
- [#7642 — Apple signin state_not_found](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/issues/7642)
- [#6207 — OAuth flow state_mismatch & state_not_found issues](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/issues/6207)
- [#5892 — `state_mismatch` persists on iPhone Chrome despite cookie config](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/issues/5892)

### Questions

1. With the configuration shown above, can you reproduce, or do you see something we are missing?
2. Why might Apple specifically and consistently end up with no verification record on callback, while Google and Discord on the same instance and same `secondaryStorage` do not?

